                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Look, I've actually played a lot longer than 11 minutes, but a quirk in how the devs set the game up means it shows as only playing a tiny fragment of the actual time played. I don't know my actual play time here either. What I do know is I've more or less finished the game before last I recall (it's been a while) and the game is a short (more like 30 minutes to an hour short, not 11 minutes short) but fun arcade-ish... rail shooter thing? I dunno, this game isn't a racing game like it sounds like it is! Does involve driving though, and does have steering that works more like an old arcade racer like Pole Position where the turns more-so push you left and right and \"turning\" kind of more-so makes you strafe. The game plays far better for it.\r\n\r\nOh yeah, and this game is also known for being very, very funny. You've probably already heard about that, but I'm going to second it.\r\n\r\nAlso the thing I like most about this game is actually the world-building myself. Despite the short runtime of the game, you can learn... quite a lot about the world the game takes place in from paying enough attention to some of the details in it. A world that's equal parts awe-inspiring and utterly horrible, somehow.\r\n\r\nI dunno I could write like a whole essay on this game but I won't, I'm just hitting recommend, saying it's good, saying it's weird and worth your time, saying it's funny and shockingly well written, and moving on.",
